    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Lisinopril works as an ACE inhibitor by blocking the conversion of angiotensin I into its potent vasoconstrictor, angiotensin II, which prevents blood vessels from narrowing. This reduction in angiotensin II levels simultaneously decreases the production of aldosterone, thereby reducing sodium and water retention in the kidneys. As a result, both systemic blood pressure and cardiac workload are lowered through these dual mechanisms on the RAAS pathway.",
