      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the ACE enzyme is blocked, Angiotensin I cannot be converted into Angiotensin II, causing a rapid drop in this potent vasoconstrictor. The body responds to this sudden deficiency by activating the Renin-Angiotensin-Aldosterone System's feedback loop, specifically the sympathetic nervous system, which triggers vasoconstriction and increased heart rate to counteract the hypotension caused by the blockade. Additionally, the absence of aldosterone leads to decreased sodium retention, while the sudden drop in blood pressure increases renin secretion to attempt (and ultimately fail) to restore the missing Angiotensin II.",
